# Build-time config for the production Vercel build.
#
# Committed on purpose. Vite inlines `VITE_*` at build time, and the Vercel
# project hosting this site belongs to another account — contributors here
# have repo write but no access to the Vercel dashboard, so committing the
# values is the only route that doesn't depend on someone else.
#
# WHAT IS AND ISN'T SECRET
#
# None of the values below is a secret. The share token is half a credential
# and ships in the client bundle regardless — anyone can read it out of the
# deployed JS. The *passcode* is the actual gate, and it is never in this
# file, in the bundle, or in the repo. The OAuth client id is a public
# client's id: it has no secret at all, and PKCE is what proves a code
# exchange belongs to the browser that started the flow.
#
# That split is what makes this file safe to commit, and it only holds while
# the passcode is strong. If the passcode is weak or has leaked, rotate it:
# BB PM → project → Share links → Manage → key icon → Generate → Save.
# Rotating does NOT change the token, so nothing here needs editing.
#
# TO TURN COMMENTS OFF
#
# Blank `VITE_BBPM_SHARE_TOKEN`. The whole comment layer compiles out and the
# site behaves exactly as it did before it existed — see `commentsConfigured`
# in `src/comments/client.ts`.
#
# TEAM SIGN-IN
#
# `VITE_BBPM_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID` adds "Continue with BB PM" next to the passcode.
# It must be registered against *this* deployed origin — the authorization
# server only redirects back to URIs on file for the client — so a new domain
# means a new registration. Blank it and the dialog quietly falls back to the
# passcode alone.
#
# Two things must be true on the API side for it to work from this origin:
#   1. `CORS_ORIGINS` includes this site's origin (the comment API is called
#      cross-origin, as it already is for the passcode flow).
#   2. The signer is a member of the SRM project in BB PM. Non-members get a
#      403 on unlock and are told to use the passcode.
#
# NEVER put a `bbpm_...` API key in here. That key is a full-account
# credential and would be readable by anyone who opens the page.

VITE_BBPM_API_BASE=https://pm.burningbros.kr/api
VITE_BBPM_SHARE_TOKEN=16574965e46951bb100306f6cc73fd52
VITE_BBPM_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
